{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d","id":53836,"title":"\u201cThe Truth\u201d","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-20T02:18:17-08:00","id":53836,"title":"\u201cThe Truth\u201d","content":"So, in the classic World of Darkness, there are many competing world-views as to what the truth of the world and cosmology may be. Is the Vampire myth the \u201cright one\u201d? The Triat? God as presented in Demon and Hunter?<br /> <br /> <br /> My question is, do you all decide what is \u201cthe truth\u201d is in your world before you run it, regardless of whether or not your players will be interacting with the world on that kind of level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T03:12:53-08:00","id":53865,"title":"","content":"I sort of have a Vampire-biased &quot;truth&quot; which lies in the background in all my campaigns, but I adjust it according to the need of each campaign. And the game we're currently playing &quot;wins&quot; when two games conflict, more often than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T03:48:44-08:00","id":53877,"title":"","content":"I like crossing over Everything. There's no single one 'truth' to my games. Everything is there and the characters can disagree with each other over it. Though far from the idea &quot;all of them are right&quot; in my world None of it has the whole story or are &quot;right&quot;. Only I know how it all fits together. Which really makes it hard for me when WW started separating the systems even more and made it so some of the cosmology directly contradicted the rest. I can't use WW's version of Demon cosmology because of this, I have to adapt it from other sources. And Hunters in my world are more like New WoD than Classic. Course I don't expect any of my players to have to know all of this stuff. None of them so far have wanted to play a Demon or a Hunter. When they do... well, guess I'll have some 'splainin to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T04:17:35-08:00","id":53885,"title":"","content":"I usually need to at least take a stance on the Demon/Vampire vs Werewolf/Mage stance, particularly on the nature of the Umbra etc.<br /> <br /> I have seen some nice attempts at using Mage-specific concepts like consensual reality to try and mash it all together, but I still can't quite get myself to use them. It somehow feels a little too.....hand-wavey ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T04:21:47-08:00","id":53887,"title":"","content":"The Umbra isn't really a problem for me. I consider all of the Vampires' dealings with spirits and their world to be considered the Low Umbra, and let Mages and Werewolves have the rest of it to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T21:35:15-08:00","id":54475,"title":"","content":"I tend to do games that have very little crossover, so the &quot;truth&quot; of the current chronicle is whichever one is appropriate to the game that's being played. Even then, it seldom, if ever, comes up directly in play and may include elements from other WoD lines or original tweaks as are appropriate to the particular story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T04:34:08-08:00","id":54599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=54475#post54475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to do games that have very little crossover, so the &quot;truth&quot; of the current chronicle is whichever one is appropriate to the game that's being played. Even then, it seldom, if ever, comes up directly in play and may include elements from other WoD lines or original tweaks as are appropriate to the particular story.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Unless you enjoy crossover and &quot;the Truth&quot; is poignant to your chronicle, I'd suggest you go with the default cosmology of the game you're running. Also, if you don't mind canon, you can always go batshit crazy and create your own secret history of the world for the game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T07:31:50-08:00","id":55430,"title":"","content":"I played mostly Mage, so that was always the dominant one for me, but the things about Mage is that since reality is subjective, it (technically) allows for all the others to be true.<br /> <br /> Demon's &quot;multi-layered reality&quot; also means all of it could be true at once, too.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, really up to the players and the STs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T07:37:58-08:00","id":55436,"title":"","content":"The truth is essentially that everything happens in some form or way, it's just a matter of what has prevalence in the lives of PC's, more or less. Reality is just layers of everything being permitted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T19:17:48-08:00","id":56526,"title":"","content":"For me, I look at each line of products as just that... &quot;lines&quot;. Within those lines, there is a common history and setting. Sometimes those lines cross, or touch, and that is when the cosmologies get messy. They all make up the greater tapestry we know as the &quot;World of Darkness&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, our personal games RARELY follow canon anyways, sooo... it's usually moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:20:56-08:00","id":56695,"title":"","content":"I remember an article in WW quarterly newsletters (back when they actually mailed the things) where they mentioned how you could alter the cosmology of the other Mystics to fit the main setting you're playing with. The examples they had were for Werewolf such as: Vampires are literally the spawn of the Wyrm that just reanimate the bodies after they person is &quot;embraced&quot;, Mages are just humans possessed by the Wyld and Hunters were created by an aspect of the Wyrm that wants to set things right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:40:09-08:00","id":56705,"title":"","content":"That's a bit simplistic in the case of Mages. After all, the Mage cosmology fits well with Garou cosmology, and the Tradition Mages are sort of the middle ground between agents of the Wyrm (Nephandi), Weaver (Technocracy) and Wyld (Marauders). I don't think Garou would miss that connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:50:14-08:00","id":56756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lubricus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=56705#post56705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a bit simplistic in the case of Mages. After all, the Mage cosmology fits well with Garou cosmology, and the Tradition Mages are sort of the middle ground between agents of the Wyrm (Nephandi), Weaver (Technocracy) and Wyld (Marauders). I don't think Garou would miss that connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Up until you start talking about space being one and the same with the spirit world, or drop the term &quot;High Umbra&quot;, to which the changers will likely respond to with the phrase, &quot;Yeah, I bet you're high, alright.&quot; Because the two cosmologies definitely do not line up on that matter, nor with a point of view on humans. Mage says that humans are the most important thing in the universe, Werewolf says that they've climbed on a pedestal that they don't deserve to be on, so feel free to kick them off.<br /> <br /> Woah there, Red Talons, I said kick, not kill.<br /> <br /> Also, while some mages might be kind of Triatic, the Traditions sure aren't Gaian. If they were, they wouldn't be practicing reality-warping in the first place. So reserve a spot in the Weaver seats for the Traditions, because they've earned it by trying to subvert reality to their own vision. Also, they're apparently very likely to encounter the OneSong and get clarified into Drones, as far as Werewolf is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T08:59:05-08:00","id":56802,"title":"","content":"I don't think Garou would be that myopic - at least not the more spiritual of them. Encountering a Mage in the Umbra, a Garou would notice how the various Spirits are reacting to the Mage's presence, and get some clues from that. Of course, that doesn't mean the Garou won't decide to kill the Mage, but that's something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:15:40-08:00","id":56922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lubricus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=56802#post56802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Garou would be that myopic - at least not the more spiritual of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside all the times that they've gone on obstinate, berserk rampages, you also have to factor in that mages are caern-raiding willworkers that deserve a swift beheading if they get near Changer territory. There's not going to be much time for comparing notes if the Fenrir rip your arms off and stuff them into your ears. Even Stargazers are going to be very hesitant to talk to you, because you warp the world in ways that endanger everyone around, and you really shouldn't be doing that, end of story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Encountering a Mage in the Umbra, a Garou would notice how the various Spirits are reacting to the Mage's presence, and get some clues from that. Of course, that doesn't mean the Garou won't decide to kill the Mage, but that's something else entirely. </div> </div> </div>They'll get clues that the mage is enslaving spirits with profane capabilities that said willworker shouldn't have. Assuming that the spirits around you are naturae, of course. Banes and strange, non-Gaian ephemera are unlikely to inspire trust if you're keeping company with them, and they won't really care how you're doing it, they will just attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:45:44-08:00","id":56940,"title":"","content":"And in a <b>Werewolf</b>-centric game, the Garou maight be <i>right</i> about mages. Just like they may be right about the claim that humanity only became what it did due to the patronage of the Weaver. <i>Not</i> assumptions I\u2019d make in a <b>Mage</b>-centric chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T12:50:01-08:00","id":56947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=56940#post56940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in a <b>Werewolf</b>-centric game, the Garou maight be <i>right</i> about mages. Just like they may be right about the claim that humanity only became what it did due to the patronage of the Weaver. <i>Not</i> assumptions I\u2019d make in a <b>Mage</b>-centric chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the strongest character is <i><b>always right!</b></i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T14:42:23-08:00","id":57014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=56940#post56940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in a <b>Werewolf</b>-centric game, the Garou maight be <i>right</i> about mages. Just like they may be right about the claim that humanity only became what it did due to the patronage of the Weaver. <i>Not</i> assumptions I\u2019d make in a <b>Mage</b>-centric chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going Mage-centric, everything about Werewolf essentially just gets chucked out of the window anyway. Hence the railing against the supposed compatibility of Mage and Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T15:00:22-08:00","id":57019,"title":"","content":"They have superficial compatability; but go beyond the fact that <b>Werewolf</b>\u2019s Triat is similar to (but not the same as) <b>Mage</b>\u2019s metaphysical trinity, and the compatability quickly falls apart. <br /> <br /> Personally, I employ a combination of ideas from <b>Demon</b> (namely, that the universe used to be a rich complex of tightly-interrelated layers of reality) and the last book of <b>Mage</b> (which suggests that the current universe is composed of multiple loosely-related layers of reality, including at least one for each gameline, where the layers are almost entirely unaware of each other but still synchronize with the others), with each layer having its own \u201cTruth\u201d \u2014 which is another way of saying that I pick one gameline for any given chronicle and interpret elements of the other gamelines through its lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T23:42:44-08:00","id":58552,"title":"","content":"Look, guys, I'm not saying that the Garou wouldn't tear any Mage they encounter apart, just that they'll probably recognise that the person they are dismembering isn't a Wyrm- or Weaver-creature. From a Werewolf's point of view, there are many other reasons to destroy people besides their Triatic orientation. After all, they tend to tear EACH OTHER apart on a semi-regular basis...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T08:00:32-08:00","id":58716,"title":"","content":"\u2026though again, in a <b>Werewolf</b>-centric chronicle, mages may in fact <i>be</i> Wyrm- or Weaver-creatures. The overarcing truth is that there <i>is</i> no overarcing truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:15:49-08:00","id":64099,"title":"","content":"I usually have my point of view already made about the truth before the game starts. I tend to use the same truth in all my games where Most God and Deities exist at the same time, some are considered lesser god while some of them are known as God to some, and demons to others. In the end though I tend to favor God as the Ultimate being and other cosmology as lesser god, or devils or other being. I also like the Idea of the Void , the Darkness before the light, and its beings predating even god itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T17:13:40-08:00","id":66854,"title":"","content":"The truth of the World of Darkness is........ shit happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T09:52:20-08:00","id":67253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=66854#post66854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth of the World of Darkness is........ shit happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire: I'm slowly descending into shit.<br /> Werewolf: The world is drowning in shit. Get a mop and bucket.<br /> Mage: It doesn't have to be shit if you don't want it to be.<br /> Wraith: Shit happens, you die, and shit gets worse.<br /> Changeling: We're going to dream our way out of this shit... wait, what am I doing again? I can't remember shit.<br /> Hunter: What the fuck is this shit?<br /> Mummy: This shit's happened before.<br /> Demon: We started this shit. No, really, please believe us!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T17:45:39-08:00","id":71747,"title":"","content":"I ran mostly Mage and Changeling, which get along pretty well provided you figure out how you're going to handle the interaction of Mages and the Dreaming. When crossovers came up, I assumed the other critters mythologies were either fabrications, or referenced things that made sense in older configurations of the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T01:00:56-08:00","id":73083,"title":"","content":"I mostly just assume that something close to the default truth of whatever game I am running for my PCs is true, with whatever modifications I need to suit my story. Sometimes I go out there with some variants, like the time I decided the Followers of Set version of the Vampire origin story was true, but whatever.<br /> <br /> Unless I play a crossover game with PCs from more than one game together. When that happens, the True History of the World of Darkness is...<br /> <br /> EXALTED!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T14:13:12-08:00","id":74549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rderekp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d#post53836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the classic World of Darkness, there are many competing world-views as to what the truth of the world and cosmology may be. Is the Vampire myth the \u201cright one\u201d? The Triat? God as presented in Demon and Hunter?<br /> <br /> <br /> My question is, do you all decide what is \u201cthe truth\u201d is in your world before you run it, regardless of whether or not your players will be interacting with the world on that kind of level?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my VTM games, the Biblical-inspired mythos of Vampire are The Truth. Although not the <i>whole </i>truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T14:42:34-08:00","id":77327,"title":"","content":"The closest thing to &quot;Truth&quot; you'll find in the World of Darkness comes in some of the later Demon supplements. Notably Days of Fire. That rather fantastic book peels back the curtain on a lot of big points.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">like the fact that God is the Abyss and that the entire point of existence was Mages. God was lonely and was looking for someone who could interact with him on his level so he created humans so that one day one might Awaken and that one day one of the Awakened might Ascend.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T08:43:59-08:00","id":77660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=77327#post77327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest thing to &quot;Truth&quot; you'll find in the World of Darkness comes in some of the later Demon supplements. Notably Days of Fire. That rather fantastic book peels back the curtain on a lot of big points.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">like the fact that God is the Abyss and that the entire point of existence was Mages. God was lonely and was looking for someone who could interact with him on his level so he created humans so that one day one might Awaken and that one day one of the Awakened might Ascend.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Referred to by the author as being more open to interpretation than a Rorschach test. No &quot;true end&quot; here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T13:53:43-08:00","id":77812,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t like the idea of the Christian God being real in my games, honestly, which is why I tend to ignore the Demon/Hunter mythos. To be honest, I don\u2019t use demons, imbued hunters or the walking dead in my Chronicles. But then I am very Werewolf-biased.<br /> <br /> <br /> However!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The idea of the Abyss actually being Heaven(s) where humans go when they die is very intriguing to me, and I may use that.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T14:15:16-08:00","id":77823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Referred to by the author as being more open to interpretation than a Rorschach test. No &quot;true end&quot; here. </div> </div> </div>\u200bCan you cite a source for that? If it's in the book I missed it, and while most of the book is vague, the part I referred to in the spoiler tag seemed pretty clear cut when Lucifer was talking about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T19:35:20-08:00","id":77991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=77823#post77823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bCan you cite a source for that? If it's in the book I missed it, and while most of the book is vague, the part I referred to in the spoiler tag seemed pretty clear cut when Lucifer was talking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?233082-Demon-The-Fallen-Days-of-Fire-for-dummies&amp;p=4989808#post4989808\" target=\"_blank\">This rpg.net post.</a><br /> <br /> And even if it describes what a being names Lucifer thinks, it matters little, since other games might just assume that he doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T19:46:22-08:00","id":77999,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I'm highly disappointed. I was really excited that it looked like someone had actually taken the giant glorious mess that is White Wolf cosmology and made a few nuggets of sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:21:21-08:00","id":78498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d?p=77999#post77999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I'm highly disappointed. I was really excited that it looked like someone had actually taken the giant glorious mess that is White Wolf cosmology and made a few nuggets of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer the glorious mess where there is no universal truth, than a truth that I don't care for (the judeo christian mythology stuff).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, my group uses The Triat as the cosmological basis for our Masquerade chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","user":"harlokin","date":". 02-24-2014, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:36:35-08:00","id":78710,"title":"","content":"I like the mess too, but I'd like there to be SOME final answer, and was very excited when I read Days of Fire because it made sense and, after all who better to know the Truth than the Demons? But it appears it was not to be. I'll keep using it in my games, but I just lost a bit of reverence for Stolze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:28:15-08:00","id":81651,"title":"","content":"Personally, I go with the notion that they are all equally true. In my opinion, Mage is the lynchpin of the whole world of darkness. The main concept of Mage is that reality is, at least in part, defined by how living conscious minds perceive it. That's the perfect in for having all of the cosmologies be equally credible. Vampires believe that the world began one way. Werewolves another. Demons believe that they helped to create the universe, and that they were righteous in their decision to interfere in the development of mankind and rebel against a distant and neglectful God. Angels, if one chooses to include them in their game in any capacity, believe that they helped to create the universe and that they were righteous in their decision to remain loyal to God and defend humanity from a prideful and reckless group of rebellious Angels who would have sought to rule over humanity as mad tyrants. All of these points of view are equally valid. All of these creation myths and ancient cosmologies have a role to play in the future of the world of darkness. They're all exactly as true as the characters and the storyteller need them to be, because magic is just works that way. The general consensus is that the universe was created via the big bang, with some vaguely Christian trappings and notions thrown on top of that by the majority of people of moderate faith. So that's the primary way everything came to be. But all of these mystical shadow histories exist just behind the veil, all metaphysical echoes of one another filtered through the perception and nature of their adherents, and they can all play apart in your story if you feel the need.<br /> <br /> At least, that's what works for me. I grew up on superhero comics, and that's how they usually handle myth and religion in their fictional universes, so it's the easiest for me to wrap my head around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T05:48:41-07:00","id":90825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rderekp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53836-\u201cthe-truth\u201d#post53836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the classic World of Darkness, there are many competing world-views as to what the truth of the world and cosmology may be. Is the Vampire myth the \u201cright one\u201d? The Triat? God as presented in Demon and Hunter? My question is, do you all decide what is \u201cthe truth\u201d is in your world before you run it, regardless of whether or not your players will be interacting with the world on that kind of level?</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest that the classic World of Darkness had to a Universal Truth was the Metaphysic Trinity of Dynamism, Stasis, Entropy, but the World of Darkness was too haphazardly created to implement any idea ubiquitously or even consistently. <br /> <br /> The mage's Avatar Essences (<i>Dynamic</i>, <i>Pattern</i>, <i>Primordial</i>) correlate to the Metaphysic Trinity (with a fourth balancing Essence, <i>Questing</i>, being the middleground of the triangle), and the three antagonist factions of the <i>Mage</i> game (Marauders, Technocrats, Nephandi) also correspond to the Metaphysic Trinity. (Extremism=Imbalance; Moderation=Balance.) The werewolves' Triat of Wyld, Weaver, Wyrm is just a theistic version of the mages' atheistic Metaphysic Trinity. Apophis is the name that mummies (and Setites) give to the Wyrm, and &quot;Grandma&quot; (&quot;Grand Maw&quot;) is the name that wraiths (and Nagaraja) give to the Wyrm. The changelings are spawns of Dynamism/Wyld. The three games which heavily employ Abrahamic mythology, <i>Vampire</i>, <i>Demon</i>, and <i>Hunter</i>, are the conceptual deviants here, but there is a Werewolf(?) book which suggests that Cain's immortality came from the Weaver (Vishnu the Preserver), and when Cain was abandoned by the Weaver he was then taken in by the Wyrm (possibly via a Wyrmish agent). This implies that the authoritarian Abrahamic god is either the authoritarian Weaver or an authoritarian spawn of the Weaver. <br /> <br /> Admittedly even the portions of the mythologies which correlate strongly are still surrounded by numerous contradictory details, but there is no other concept in the classic World of Darkness that comes as close to a Universal Truth as the Metaphysic Trinity. <br /> <br /> White Wolf's biggest mistake, apart from not ubiquitously and consistently implementing the Metaphysic Trinity, was hastily cramming the various supernatural populations onto a single planet and then clumsily backpedaling to erect and maintain extremely contrived separations that strain credibility. White Wolf should have either consistently utilized the Metaphysic Trinity as a background tenet for knitting all of the games into a cohesive whole (even if not done in a readily obvious way) or they should have utilized a multiple parallel Earths cosmology to sanely keep the games separate; instead they blindly took a middle road which resulted in a sloppily conceived world the whole of which can only be held in a schizophrenic mind. (In another post I will offer my resolution to the contradiction of having such powerhouses as the Methuselahs, Maruaders, Technocracy, and Pentex all on the same planet yet somehow incredulously not stepping on each others's toes way more often.)<br /> <br /> Despite my complaints about the schizophrenia of the classic World of Darkness, the Triat is my favorite pantheon of any fictional universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:02:43-07:00","id":93411,"title":"","content":"The truth is subjective in my chronicles. It's all about interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}